input_only: False
instruction: 'Design a survey comprising 10-15 quantitative and qualitative questions that inquire about the overall customer service experience, product or service satisfaction, ease of communication with the company, and suggestions for future improvements. The survey should be easy to understand, well-organized, and aesthetically pleasing. Consider using Likert scales, open-ended questions, multiple-choice, and demographic questions to gain insights into your customer base.'
target: '1. How satisfied are you with the overall customer service experience provided by our company?\n2. How likely are you to recommend our product/service to a friend or colleague?\n3. How satisfied are you with the quality of our product/service?\n4. How often do you use our product/service?\n5. Have you had any issues with our product/service? If yes, how were they resolved?\n6. How easy was it to communicate with our company (e.g, phone, email, live chat, social media)?\n7. How satisfied were you with the response time to your inquiries or concerns?\n8. How would you rate the professionalism of our customer service representatives?\n9. In your opinion, how could our company improve your customer service experience?\n10. Did our company meet your expectations? If no, please explain.\n11. Which aspect of our product/service did you like the most?\n12. Which aspect of our product/service did you like the least?\n13. What other services or products would you like to see from our company?\n14. What age bracket do you fall under?\n15. What is your level of education? \n\nLikert scale questions:\n1. How strongly do you agree/disagree with the following statement: Our company provides excellent customer service.\n2. How strongly do you agree/disagree with the following statement: Our product/service met my expectations.\n3. How strongly do you agree/disagree with the following statement: I found it easy to communicate with our company.\n\nMultiple-choice questions:\n1. What motivated you to purchase our product/service? (Multiple answers allowed)\n    a. Price\n    b. Quality\n    c. Reviews\n    d. Recommendation from a friend/colleague\n    e. Other (please specify)\n2. How did you first hear about our product/service?\n    a. Social media\n    b. Online search\n    c. Word of mouth\n    d. Other (please specify)'
formatted_prompt: "<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nDesign a survey comprising 10-15 quantitative and qualitative questions that inquire about the overall customer service experience, product or service satisfaction, ease of communication with the company, and suggestions for future improvements. The survey should be easy to understand, well-organized, and aesthetically pleasing. Consider using Likert scales, open-ended questions, multiple-choice, and demographic questions to gain insights into your customer base.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n1. How satisfied are you with the overall customer service experience provided by our company?\n2. How likely are you to recommend our product/service to a friend or colleague?\n3. How satisfied are you with the quality of our product/service?\n4. How often do you use our product/service?\n5. Have you had any issues with our product/service? If yes, how were they resolved?\n6. How easy was it to communicate with our company (e.g, phone, email, live chat, social media)?\n7. How satisfied were you with the response time to your inquiries or concerns?\n8. How would you rate the professionalism of our customer service representatives?\n9. In your opinion, how could our company improve your customer service experience?\n10. Did our company meet your expectations? If no, please explain.\n11. Which aspect of our product/service did you like the most?\n12. Which aspect of our product/service did you like the least?\n13. What other services or products would you like to see from our company?\n14. What age bracket do you fall under?\n15. What is your level of education? \n\nLikert scale questions:\n1. How strongly do you agree/disagree with the following statement: Our company provides excellent customer service.\n2. How strongly do you agree/disagree with the following statement: Our product/service met my expectations.\n3. How strongly do you agree/disagree with the following statement: I found it easy to communicate with our company.\n\nMultiple-choice questions:\n1. What motivated you to purchase our product/service? (Multiple answers allowed)\n    a. Price\n    b. Quality\n    c. Reviews\n    d. Recommendation from a friend/colleague\n    e. Other (please specify)\n2. How did you first hear about our product/service?\n    a. Social media\n    b. Online search\n    c. Word of mouth\n    d. Other (please specify)<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nThis is a great start for the survey, but can you add some questions about the website usability and navigation? Also, can we include a question about the delivery time?<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nSure, here are some additional questions addressing website usability, navigation, and delivery time:\n\n1. How easy was it to navigate our website?\n2. Did you find the information you were looking for on our website?\n3. Did you encounter any issues while using our website? If so, please describe.\n4. How satisfied are you with the layout and design of our website?\n5. Were you able to complete your desired action on our website? (e.g., place an order, contact our customer service, etc.)\n6. How satisfied are you with the delivery time of your product/service?\n7. Was the estimated delivery time communicated clearly during the ordering process?\n8. Did you encounter any issues with the delivery process? If so, please describe.\n9. How likely are you to purchase from our website again in the future?\n10. How could our website be improved to better meet your needs?\n11. How likely are you to recommend our website to others?\n\nLikert scale questions:\n1. How easy was it to find what you were looking for on our website?\n2. How satisfied were you with the delivery time of your product/service?\n3. How strongly do you agree/disagree with the following statement: Our website is user-friendly.\n\nMultiple-choice questions:\n1. How did you access our website? (Multiple answers allowed)\n    a. Desktop\n    b. Mobile phone\n    c. Tablet\n2. On a scale of 1-10, how likely are you to recommend our product/service to a friend or colleague?\n3. On a scale of 1-10, how likely are you to recommend our website to a friend or colleague?<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nThanks for adding those questions about the website usability and delivery time. Can you also include a question regarding the pricing of our product/service? I think it will help us understand how our customers perceive the value we offer.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nSure, here is a question addressing the pricing of your product/service:\n\n1. How would you rate the value for money of our product/service? \n\nLikert scale question:\n1. How satisfied are you with the pricing of our product/service?\n\nMultiple-choice question:\n1. How did you find our product/service pricing in comparison to our competitors? \n    a. Significantly more expensive\n    b. Slightly more expensive\n    c. About the same\n    d. Slightly less expensive\n    e. Significantly less expensive<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nThanks for incorporating my request for a question about the pricing of our product/service. However, can we add another question to understand how our customers perceive the quality of our customer service representatives? I think it will help us identify areas of improvement in our training and hiring processes.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nSure, here's an additional question that addresses the quality of customer service representatives:\n\n1. How satisfied are you with the knowledge and helpfulness of our customer service representatives?\n\nLikert scale question:\n1. How satisfied are you with the overall quality of our customer service representatives?\n\nMultiple-choice question:\n1. How frequently do you interact with our customer service representatives?\n    a. Frequently\n    b. Occasionally\n    c. Rarely\n    d. Never\n\nOpen-ended question:\n1. Is there a specific customer service representative or interaction that stood out positively or negatively? If so, please share your experience."
