input_only: False
instruction: "Here is a piece of text: Extracts the Instaviz diagrams from the user's iPhone or iPod Touch backups. The user can then choose to print the diagrams or export them to any of these vector and bitmap formats: BMP, EMF, GIF, Graphviz, JPEG, PNG, SVG, TIFF, VML or Visio VDX. Instaviz is an iPhone/iPod Touch app that turns roughly sketched shapes and lines into beautifully laid-out graphs. The app is great for drawing mind maps, concept maps, flowcharts and graph theory, or just simple note-taking and brainstorming. Version 1.4 fixes graphs not appearing from iTunes 8.2 backups.\n\nBased on the text material above, generate the response to the following quesion or instruction: How can I export my Instaviz diagrams to other formats, and what formats are available?"
target: 'You can export your Instaviz diagrams to various vector and bitmap file formats such as BMP, EMF, GIF, Graphviz, JPEG, PNG, SVG, TIFF, VML or Visio VDX. You can choose to print the diagrams or export them from your iPhone or iPod Touch backups. Instaviz is a useful app for creating mind maps, flowcharts, and graph theory diagrams. Additionally, version 1.4 addresses an issue with graphs not appearing in iTunes 8.2 backups.'
formatted_prompt: '<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nHere is a piece of text: Extracts the Instaviz diagrams from the user\'s iPhone or iPod Touch backups. The user can then choose to print the diagrams or export them to any of these vector and bitmap formats: BMP, EMF, GIF, Graphviz, JPEG, PNG, SVG, TIFF, VML or Visio VDX. Instaviz is an iPhone/iPod Touch app that turns roughly sketched shapes and lines into beautifully laid-out graphs. The app is great for drawing mind maps, concept maps, flowcharts and graph theory, or just simple note-taking and brainstorming. Version 1.4 fixes graphs not appearing from iTunes 8.2 backups.\n\nBased on the text material above, generate the response to the following quesion or instruction: How can I export my Instaviz diagrams to other formats, and what formats are available?<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nYou can export your Instaviz diagrams to various vector and bitmap file formats such as BMP, EMF, GIF, Graphviz, JPEG, PNG, SVG, TIFF, VML or Visio VDX. You can choose to print the diagrams or export them from your iPhone or iPod Touch backups. Instaviz is a useful app for creating mind maps, flowcharts, and graph theory diagrams. Additionally, version 1.4 addresses an issue with graphs not appearing in iTunes 8.2 backups.<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nCan you please guide me on how to extract the Instaviz diagrams from my iPhone backups?<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nSure! Here is a step-by-step guide to extract the Instaviz diagrams from your iPhone backups:\n\n1. Connect your iPhone or iPod Touch to your computer.\n\n2. Open iTunes and select your device.\n\n3. Under the "Backups" section, click on "Restore Backup."\n\n4. Choose the backup file that contains the Instaviz diagrams you want to extract.\n\n5. Once the restore is finished, download and install a backup extractor tool such as iBackup Extractor or iPhone Backup Extractor.\n\n6. Open the backup extractor tool and select your device and backup file.\n\n7. Look for the Instaviz app in the list of apps and select it.\n\n8. The tool should display a list of files associated with Instaviz. Look for the files with the ".dot" extension; these are the Instaviz diagrams.\n\n9. Select the files you want to extract and choose the export format you want (e.g., PNG, SVG, etc.)\n\n10. Save the files to your computer or another device.\n\nThat\'s it! You should now have your Instaviz diagrams in the format you wanted.'
